      "final_text": "Done. The task is verified end to end.\n\n**Root cause:** [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) ran only six Newton steps instead of the deployed seven, so large inputs converged one iteration short (e.g. `2^256 - 1` came out 198202503 below the true floor).\n\n**Fix:** restored the seventh `(result + a / result) >>> 1` line, matching `newtonSqrt 7`. Then proved the routine returns the exact floor for every 256-bit input:\n- The `log2`-based estimate `2^(log2(a)/2)` starts at or below the root and within a factor of two above it.\n- After the first step all iterates stay at/above the root and fit in 129 bits, so each word-level step (with the final `min`) is exactly the Nat-level Newton step \u2014 via `ProofForgeFin.WordBridge.iter_map_of_sim`.\n- Seven steps suffice by the library's `newtonIter_eq_or_succ_of_lt_two_mul` with `b = 128, k = 5`, closed by `min_div_eq_sqrt`.\n\nAll 8 required theorems (`req_sqrt_not_above/below`, `req_sqrt_up_covers/tight`, `req_mint_backed/full/live`, `req_newton_budget`) are proved with the exact locked statements, no `sorry`, no forbidden constructs, only permitted axioms.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `lake build Solution`: 8 of 8 proved.\n- `check_candidate`: `\"status\": \"VERIFIED\"` \u2014 all requirements VERIFIED across all six kernels, executable property tests PASS (2001 cases). Passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json`, sha256 `d893922c\u20267f84262e`.\n- `verify_passport`: reproduced.",
